drm/amd/display: display power backports for the GA605 OLED eDP (dev build)

Three backports, combined (default behaviour unchanged unless noted):
  1. disable self-refresh on tearing flips (upstream 2e54a92e0136; also in
     7.2.11 stable, drop once the base is >= 7.2.11)
  2. tear down a dangling pipe on boot to fix s0i3 (mainline 98e08a815ef6)
  3. CACP for OLED eDP, hand-ported from 7b0cc3085216: adds
     card*-eDP-1/amdgpu/panel_power_savings (0-4), boots at 0 (off). Nothing in
     this package changes that level.

Compile-tested only (amdgpu objects, 0 warnings); not booted yet. Not for
upstream submission.

---
amdgpu display power backports from 7.3 / amd-staging-drm-next for linux-omarchy 7.2.8

Applies with `patch -Np1 --fuzz=0` after 0480 (or anywhere after the amd
display patches 0450-0480). Contents, in order:

1. drm/amd/display: disable self-refresh on tearing flips
   stable 7.2.11 04ee82fec489 (upstream 2e54a92e0136, staging 667ef5fff9)
2. drm/amd/display: Tear down dangling pipe on boot to fix s0i3
   upstream 98e08a815ef6 (v7.3-rc1; staging 73fcabe89f86), context-only backport
3. drm/amd/display: Enable CACP on Linux
   upstream 7b0cc3085216 (v7.3-rc1), hunks for amdgpu_dm_backlight.c and
   amdgpu_dm_connector.c ported to amdgpu_dm.c; dmub_flush_buffer_mem() kept

Individual git-format patches with full commit messages are next to this file.
Compile-tested (amdgpu objects, gcc 16.2.1, running 7.2.8-9-omarchy config).

